.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tine-run 1  "run " 
.SH NAME
tine\-run \- Group writes into a git run: each write made with `\-\-run ID` is committed (after a snapshot of your own pending edits), and the run can be squashed or reverted as one
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtine run\fR [\fB\-\-debug\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Group writes into a git run: each write made with `\-\-run ID` is committed (after a snapshot of your own pending edits), and the run can be squashed or reverted as one
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-debug\fR
Enable diagnostic logging for the desktop app
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tine\-run\-begin(1)
Check the graph\*(Aqs git repository and print a new run id
.TP
tine\-run\-show(1)
List the run\*(Aqs commits
.TP
tine\-run\-end(1)
Squash the run into one commit when none of it is pushed, branched or interleaved with other commits; otherwise leave it as it is
.TP
tine\-run\-revert(1)
Undo the run\*(Aqs edits, newest first. A block you changed since keeps your text and is listed
